    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">longaevus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		longus-aevum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of great age, aged, ancient</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">parens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 169</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 525</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 715</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 1, 52: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 10, 864</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senecta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 10, 47</span></i>
			 (3, 5, 31): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vetustas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Spect. 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">longaeva</span></b> , ae, f., <i>an old woman</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cunctantem longaeva manu deducit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 462</span></i>
			.</div>
